# NOITE's gym (4fsalgin) starts the real SALGIN, which wins: NOITE gets
# 0x40c (hides), then 0x40a, shows itself, adds the score and goes to the
# garden cutscene (espquete, which starts JARDIM).
#
#   zig-out/bin/noite --headless --scene 4fsalgin --ms 72000 --input tools/play/salgin-4fsalgin-win.input
#   zig-out/bin/noite --headless --scene 4fsalgin --ms 80000 --fix all --input tools/play/salgin-4fsalgin-win.input
#
# The sportsman's animation ends at 8733 (the WinExec); SALGIN starts 1500
# ms later (10233). Up is held from 11000 (salgin-alone-win.input): the KO
# is on the beat at 61233 in both versions, the window closes at 65333.
# The Original's player keeps 83 energy (+8300), the Corrigida's 85
# (+8500: S5's single seed picks other attacks).
# The Corrigida (`--fix all`) shows SALGIN's controls screen first; Enter takes
# it down 50 ms after it opened, PORRADA stands for 2 s (the frozen intro,
# `fight_controls.start_delay_ms`) and the round then plays as the
# Original's from its start, 2050 ms later (`delay`: every later line
# moves too).
# Its keys are the new layout: S is the flying kick (voadora) (the Original's Up).
0 ?fight_keys_asdf keymap up s
10283 ?fight_controls_screen key return
10283 ?fight_controls_screen delay 2050
10500 dump gym
11000 !fight_fair hold up 52000
12000 !fight_fair dump fight
